# Data Architecture: Sanity vs Hardcoded

## Content Split Rule

| Content | Source | Reason |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Articles | Sanity | Villagers publish via WYSIWYG |
| Categories | Sanity | Referenced by articles |
| Homestays | Hardcoded | Villagers cannot edit |
| Attractions | Hardcoded | Villagers cannot edit |
| Booklet | Hardcoded | Villagers cannot edit |
| Downloads | Hardcoded | Villagers cannot edit |

## Required TypeScript Interfaces

### Homestay

```typescript
// data/homestays.ts
import { StaticImageData } from 'next/image'

export interface Homestay {
  id: string
  name_id: string
  name_en: string
  description_id: string
  description_en: string
  photos: StaticImageData[]  // Static imports for next/image optimization
  priceRange: string         // e.g., "Rp 200.000 - 350.000 / malam"
  facilities: string[]       // e.g., ["WiFi", "AC", "Breakfast"]
  whatsappNumber: string     // e.g., "6281234567890"
}

// Example entry
import photo1 from '@/public/images/homestays/villa-sunrise-1.jpg'
import photo2 from '@/public/images/homestays/villa-sunrise-2.jpg'

export const homestays: Homestay[] = [
  {
    id: 'villa-sunrise',
    name_id: 'Villa Sunrise',
    name_en: 'Villa Sunrise',
    description_id: 'Penginapan nyaman dengan pemandangan matahari terbit',
    description_en: 'Comfortable lodging with sunrise view',
    photos: [photo1, photo2],
    priceRange: 'Rp 250.000 - 400.000 / malam',
    facilities: ['WiFi', 'AC', 'Sarapan', 'Parkir'],
    whatsappNumber: '6281234567890',
  },
]
```

